# Crag: cragd, the device configuration API daemon (docs/06, M3 — the
# real Zig daemon in the graph position the M1 health-check stub held,
# docs/02 §5.1). Runs unprivileged (docs/02 §7): listeners are
# /run/crag/cragd.sock (gated by the crag-api group on the parent dir)
# and 127.0.0.1:8080 (bearer token; recorded deviation from docs/06's :80).
#
# "started" = readiness: the daemon writes one byte to fd 4 once both
# listeners are bound (--ready-fd), so boot-success — and rauc-mark-good
# behind it — only fire when the API is actually reachable.
#
# depends-on rationale:
#   data-mount    hard: mutable-state layer failure must fail cragd and,
#                 through it, boot-success (rollback semantics, AD-011)
#   firstboot     bakes /data/config/{api-token,crag.json} before the
#                 daemon first reads them
#   local.target  orders early-tmpfiles first: it creates /run/crag
#                 (tmpfiles.d/cragd.conf) and opens /run/dinitctl to the
#                 cragd group for the reboot/poweroff endpoints
#   dbus-daemon   hard (docs/02 §5.1): the D-Bus spine (RAUC now, iwd in
#                 phase 3) needs the system bus socket; without it the
#                 update/network groups can only 503
#   rauc          waits-for, not depends-on: cragd degrades cleanly
#                 (503 rauc-unavailable + restart re-attach probe) if
#                 rauc is down, and must not be pulled down with it
#   iwd, dhcpcd   waits-for (soft — docs/02 §5.1): the phase-3 network
#                 group wants both up before cragd snapshots the iwd
#                 tree and first-renders /run/crag/net/dhcpcd.conf, but
#                 cragd is control plane: it must neither pull the data
#                 plane down with it nor refuse to start when a radio-less
#                 board has iwd sitting idle or dhcpcd failed. Also the
#                 reverse dependency is forbidden: dhcpcd/iwd never wait
#                 for cragd (see the dhcpcd shadow's bootstrap notes).

type = process
command = /usr/bin/cragd --ready-fd=4
ready-notification = pipefd:4
run-as = cragd
restart = true
logfile = /var/log/cragd.log
depends-on: data-mount
depends-on: firstboot
depends-on: local.target
depends-on: dbus-daemon
waits-for: rauc
waits-for: iwd
waits-for: dhcpcd
